Third-party material

1. Adreno740, formerly NativeAdreno (MIT)
   Copyright (c) 2026 NativeAdreno contributors
   https://github.com/UniXNU/Adreno740/tree/5c8c1453c67d6ef6b10ec43ab1f8fc570a2f33e1
   (pinned commit; the repository was renamed, its files keep the NativeAdreno
   prefix).
   Reference copies: Adreno740-main/ and NativeAdreno-reference-old/ (verbatim,
   not built, not committed, keep their own MIT headers). Used as the model for
   module structure, error handling, the user-client ABI shape and the
   host-test style. Files of this project that are derived from it say so in
   their header; NativeMaliHandleIndex.h keeps its MIT header. The XNU adapters
   under xnu/ follow its IOKit call shapes (window mapping, buffer allocation
   and span walking, the cache-maintenance sequence, the BO view cache) and are
   derived from it in that sense.

2. Linux kernel: drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/, drivers/iommu/io-pgtable-arm.c,
   include/uapi/drm/panfrost_drm.h, Documentation/devicetree/bindings/gpu/
   arm,mali-bifrost.yaml
   SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0 / GPL-2.0-only (per file)
   Reference copy: third_party/linux-panfrost/ (verbatim, not built, keeps its
   own SPDX headers and copyrights; byte-identical to torvalds/linux at commit
   9944dd07f3cf7b6c19d65c2585147887ca06677c).
   Source of every register offset, bit definition and page-table format used
   here; each converted value names the file and function it came from. Pinned in
   third_party/PINNED.md.

3. Mesa (MIT)
   Copyright (C) 2019-2020 Collabora Ltd., Alyssa Rosenzweig, Broadcom
   Reference copy: third_party/mesa-panfrost/ (verbatim, not built):
     src/panfrost/genxml/v7.xml   Bifrost v7 descriptor bit layout (M6)
     src/panfrost/lib/pan_jc.h    the job-chain builder and header fields
   Read as a specification; the job header's own bit positions still need
   common.xml, so that part of the driver stays a marked TODO.

4. Device tree: tests/data/mt6768.dtb is the device tree of the owner's phone
   (MediaTek, vendor tree). It is board data, not code; it is used only as test
   input and as the source of the DT facts quoted in the driver comments.

5. MediaTek vendor kernel (GPL-2.0 / GPL-2.0-only, per file)
   Reference copy: third_party/mtk-android/ (verbatim, not built, not committed;
   extracted from the owner's phone's GPL kernel archive). Source of every M2
   offset, bit and voltage value: clk-mt6768-pg.c, clk-mt6768.c,
   mt6358-regulator.c, pwrap_hal.[ch], upmu_hw.h, mtk_gpufreq_core.[ch] and the
   MT6768 board DTS. Each value used by the driver names the file and the
   function or line it came from; docs/MTK_SOURCES.md records the sha256 of each
   file so a different archive is detected rather than silently trusted.

